abstract: >-
  Governed Signal-to-Content is a local-first reference implementation for
  monitoring external technical developments, preserving source evidence,
  evaluating structural relevance, and generating reusable content artifacts
  inside a deterministic governance workflow. The system separates
  probabilistic or human-assisted interpretation from authoritative state
  transitions. Publication remains subject to explicit human approval, while
  evidence identity, workflow state, and execution receipts remain durable and
  inspectable.
